From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:21:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: require c++20 for pytorch 2.13+

Upstream already fixed this (nihui/ncnn@61ea75123d0ea71e4b029742664e3d49b7c8eec6,
merged 2026-09-17), but this port pins pnnx at a commit from before that fix
(2026-05-26, matching the 20260526 PyPI release date). The riscv64 torch wheels
this repo publishes are 2.13.0+cpu and 2.14.0+cpu, both >= 2.13, so without this
backport the build fails: ATen's headers at torch>=2.13 require a C++20
compiler, and the unpatched CMakeLists.txt here only ever requests C++17.

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://github.com/Tencent/ncnn/commit/61ea75123d0ea71e4b029742664e3d49b7c8eec6]
---
 tools/pnnx/CMakeLists.txt | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/tools/pnnx/CMakeLists.txt b/tools/pnnx/CMakeLists.txt
index e50ab47..210eb73 100644
--- a/tools/pnnx/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tools/pnnx/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -59,7 +59,10 @@ if(Torch_VERSION VERSION_LESS "1.8")
     message(FATAL_ERROR "pnnx only supports PyTorch >= 1.8")
 endif()
 
-if(Torch_VERSION VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL "2.1")
+if(Torch_VERSION VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL "2.13")
+    # c++20 is required for using torch 2.13+ headers
+    set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 20)
+elseif(Torch_VERSION VERSION_GREATER_EQUAL "2.1")
     # c++17 is required for using torch 2.1+ headers
     set(CMAKE_CXX_STANDARD 17)
 endif()
-- 
